// Contracts that are accepted, proved — and wrong.
//
// Every function in this package passes `moon prove`. Every one of them is
// also broken, and the tests alongside them say how. They are here because
// each is a property of the verifier rather than of the program, none is in
// the manual, and each cost real time to find.
//
// The common shape: the solver reasons about *mathematical* integers, and the
// machine does not. A proof is a proof about the model it was stated in, and
// the gap between that model and the hardware has to be closed by hand.
options(
  "proof-enabled": true,
)
